-## 1. Architectural Principles & Core Tenets
-
-### 1.1 Deterministic Pricing (Zero AI Hallucination)
-- In the travel industry, pricing errors result in severe financial losses or breached supplier contracts. Dalil enforces an uncompromised separation of concerns:
-  - **AI's Role**: Information extraction, intent parsing, semantic parameter mapping, and multilingual translation.
-  - **Pricing Engine's Role**: 100% deterministic mathematical calculations. Every single line item must resolve to a contracted supplier rate in the database matching season, room category, occupancy basis, and nationality tier.
-  - If any rate is missing from the library, the system explicitly marks the line item as `Rate Missing` and enforces a hard guardrail preventing dispatch until resolved.
-
-### 1.2 Non-Custodial Operations (Zero Payment Handling)
-- Dalil never collects, escrows, charges, or holds traveler or agent funds.
-- Proposals present verified static bank wire instructions (IBAN, Swift/BIC) or official on-arrival cash collection terms.
-- Subscription plans are purely descriptive licensing tiers without billing gateway overhead.
-
-### 1.3 Human-in-the-Loop AI Verification
-- Client messages from WhatsApp or email can be noisy, ambiguous, or contain sensitive information.
-- Inbound inquiries are sanitized to mask passport numbers, card digits, or credentials.
-- A side-by-side review drawer presents original raw inputs adjacent to extracted JSON parameters, allowing the operations agent to confirm or amend values before generating an itinerary.
-
-### 1.4 Strict Multi-Tenant Isolation & Granular RBAC
-- Every record is segregated by `workspaceId`.
-- Access levels: `Owner`, `Admin`, `Sales Agent`, `Operations`, `Viewer`.
-- **"Hide Net Costs from Sales Agents"**: When enabled, sales representatives only see sell prices and markup percentages, protecting confidential wholesale supplier contracts.
-
-### 1.5 Native Bilingualism with Full RTL Mirroring
-- The application natively supports **English** and **Arabic (عربي)**.
-- Selecting Arabic automatically triggers bidirectional layout mirroring (`dir="rtl"`), font optimization, inverted iconography, and adapted padding across all modals, tables, and print outputs.
